{"id":"852a0356bca26d3a","group":"89","path":"89/89-thm-convergence-completeness.md","title":"Completeness for Convergence Logics","display":"thm-convergence-completeness — Completeness for Convergence Logics","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-thm-convergence-completeness","aliases":["89-thm-convergence-completeness"],"created":"2026-10-05","display":"thm-convergence-completeness — Completeness for Convergence Logics","depends_on":["[[89-df-convergence-logic]]","[[89-thm-convergence-soundness]]","[[89-thm-canonical-convergence]]","[[89-thm-canonical-model]]","[[89-df-valid-modal]]"],"revised":"2026-10-05"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-thm-convergence-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-thm-convergence-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"created","html":"2026-10-05"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-convergence-completeness — Completeness for Convergence Logics"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"42a3ef8675246492\" href=\"?note=42a3ef8675246492\" title=\"89-df-convergence-logic\">89-df-convergence-logic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"716a176673d9ea45\" href=\"?note=716a176673d9ea45\" title=\"89-thm-convergence-soundness\">89-thm-convergence-soundness</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a668d880013388bd\" href=\"?note=a668d880013388bd\" title=\"89-thm-canonical-convergence\">89-thm-canonical-convergence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d5bc3d5ff97b8f74\" href=\"?note=d5bc3d5ff97b8f74\" title=\"89-thm-canonical-model\">89-thm-canonical-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"dbba58e7bd3b0667\" href=\"?note=dbba58e7bd3b0667\" title=\"89-df-valid-modal\">89-df-valid-modal</a></span></div>"},{"key":"revised","html":"2026-10-05"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\subseteq\\omega^4\">\\(a\\subseteq\\omega^4\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\">\\(A\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_{\\Box}\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm K_a\">\\(\\mathrm K_a\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Conv}_a\">\\(\\mathrm{Conv}_a\\)</span> 取收敛逻辑定义。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> 遍历非空 Kripke 框架，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\\models A\">\\(F\\models A\\)</span> 量化所有赋值和世界。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}convergence\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\nA\\in\\mathrm K_a\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\forall F\\;(\\mathrm{Conv}_a(F)\\to F\\models A).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}convergence\\text{-}completeness}\\vdash\nA\\in\\mathrm K_a\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\forall F\\;(\\mathrm{Conv}_a(F)\\to F\\models A).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Boolos, <em>The Logic of Provability</em>，印刷页 89–90；对应 PDF 页为印刷页加 39。</p>\n<p>在任意 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span>-收敛框架上，所有额外模式有效；K、MP、必然化与统一替换在框架有效性下保持，得到正向。逆向：<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm K_a\">\\(\\mathrm K_a\\)</span> 一致正规，它的典范框架对每个 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span> 中四元组收敛。因此若右侧成立，特别在典范模型的赋值下成立；典范模型定理得到 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathrm K_a\">\\(A\\in\\mathrm K_a\\)</span>。这是第 6 章 Theorem 3，不将 GL 错误列入这一公理家族。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},